  "notes": [
    "The tenth and last Upgraded(address) event before the incident selected implementation 0xb28723a16d3347cdc0ce035eb1c1eb0b7406682f. The proxy's EIP-1967 implementation slot holds that address immediately before the anchor, and the anchor delegates addLiquidity(address,uint160) to it.",
    "Gross depletion is the WBNB transferred out of 68 attacker-preinitialized PancakeSwap V3 pools in their first post-migration drain, summed over 66 transactions. WBNB Transfer, Deposit and Withdrawal logs show no WBNB input to those pools in the selected transactions, so the exact aggregate outflow is also their aggregate transaction-level balance decrease. Eighteen attacker-created pools that never migrated and six migrated pools with no drain during the campaign are excluded. The public 287 BNB / USD 183,000 estimate is not used because it does not reconcile to gross pool depletion. No recovery is netted."
